WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.600
So today I thought we'd take a little bit
of a deeper look at Joe Biden's 2020 platform.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.180
And I don't just want to read through his
positions.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:14.990
What I want to do is pick a few areas and
think about whether Joe Biden's ideas, whether

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:19.580
Joe Biden's policy positions, his policy prescriptions,
his platform.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:29.689
Would Joe Biden's policy ideas really deal
with root problems or would they fix symptoms

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:31.140
of a problem?

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.710
And I want to make a couple of things clear.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:40.570
Number one, we have a system that incentivizes
dealing with symptoms and not problems when

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:41.710
you're in Congress.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.260
You have a reelection every two years and
you have to justify being reelected.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.960
Presidents have four year terms, senators
six.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:54.780
But of course, it's much more difficult to
get big things done sometimes in the Senate,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.680
depending on what type of thing you're talking
about.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.410
Although that doesn't always apply.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:04.129
So we fundamentally have a system that encourages
not really dealing with the systemic problems

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:09.520
which often take more than two or four years
to deal with, but rather dealing with symptoms

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.369
or even appearing to deal with symptoms without
actually dealing with them.

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:15.700
So we're going to talk about that now.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.610
A few important things to think about.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.119
One is I'm going to go by Joe Biden stated
2020 platform.

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:26.280
Now there are going to be people who write
to me and say, I don't believe that Joe Biden

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.579
actually wants to do X or Y, even though he
claims he does listen to some extent.

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:34.639
No president does what they promise.

00:01:34.639 --> 00:01:40.729
And every candidate states that they will
try to do things that are very difficult to

00:01:40.729 --> 00:01:42.369
do or almost impossible to do.

00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:45.239
Look at Donald Trump's presidency for an example.

00:01:45.239 --> 00:01:46.719
But this is a pointless exercise.

00:01:46.719 --> 00:01:50.599
If we're simply going to say, oh, here's Joe's
list of stuff he wants to do.

00:01:50.599 --> 00:01:51.649
I think he's just lying.

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:52.649
OK.

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:56.599
I mean, listen, that that's it's impossible
to defeat that argument if you want to insist

00:01:56.599 --> 00:01:59.079
on making it number two.

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:02.169
Some of you might say, well, why aren't you
talking about Biden wanting to cut Social

00:02:02.169 --> 00:02:03.169
Security?

00:02:03.169 --> 00:02:09.580
Again, I'm going by Biden's 2020 platform
in the 90s, Joe Biden said he would consider

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:14.300
putting Social Security cuts on the table
if a proposal otherwise made sense to him.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.430
It was 25 years ago.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.860
It's not part of his platform today.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:21.099
There's no real reason to include that in
his platform because it's simply not.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:25.989
Lastly, when I talk about solving a problem
versus dealing with the symptom, let's use

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:29.459
an example from the Trump presidency.

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:33.799
Trump believes the solution to undocumented
immigration is to build a wall across the

00:02:33.799 --> 00:02:36.459
entire u.s.-mexico border.

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:39.269
Building a wall at best deals with a symptom.

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:40.269
Right.

00:02:40.269 --> 00:02:45.080
The wall would potentially slow down the portion
of people coming to the U.S. illegally by

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.750
physically crossing the u.s.-mexico land border.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.810
That's a symptom of the problem to solve the
actual problem.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:55.330
You would have to deal with, number one, the
economic conditions in Latin America that

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:59.120
lead people to want to come to the United
States illegally in the first place.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.569
You would have to deal with more strictly
punishing or punishing at all companies that

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:07.260
hire undocumented immigrants, because as long
as companies keep doing that and not being

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.220
punished, they're going to continue doing
it.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.530
And number three, you would also have to account
for the higher prices that would come on many

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:18.450
products if indeed you rooted out all undocumented
labor in the United States.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:23.840
So building the wall may be addressed as part
of one symptom, but it does nothing to deal

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.870
with the problem.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.540
That's the type of thinking that we want to
do here.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.569
I'm not going to do all of Joe Biden's positions,
but let's do some of the key things.

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:34.489
We'll start with criminal justice on criminal
justice.

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:41.099
Joe Biden wants to eliminate mandatory minimum
sentences, eliminate private prisons and the

00:03:41.099 --> 00:03:47.090
cocaine sentencing disparity, end the cash
bail system and eliminate the death penalty.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:52.569
So to answer whether this deals with the problem
or just symptoms, you have to understand what

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:54.400
the problem is.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.599
I would generalize the problem with our justice
system, including the courts and criminal

00:03:59.599 --> 00:04:06.010
justice system, as we have a two tiered system,
one for the rich and one for the poor with

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:12.889
a heavily racialized component and a for profit
component that has no business being there.

00:04:12.889 --> 00:04:18.359
And it is at its core, a system that is focusing
too much on street crime and not enough on

00:04:18.359 --> 00:04:20.760
corporate and white collar crime.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.750
So when I look at what Joe Biden wants to
do on criminal justice, I would say that this

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:30.470
is somewhere in the middle between fixing
symptoms and dealing with the problem.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.970
Biden goes directly at some elements of the
problem.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:39.099
So ending cash bail in private prisons that
deals with the for profit component of the

00:04:39.099 --> 00:04:40.310
problem.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.000
But the problem is way bigger.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.889
And this proposal from Joe Biden does nothing
about setting priorities in terms of street

00:04:47.889 --> 00:04:51.449
crime versus corporate and white collar crime.

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:52.639
Doesn't address that at all.

00:04:52.639 --> 00:04:56.870
Biden also is not in favor of legalization
of cannabis.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:59.430
That is a massive criminal justice issue.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.220
And he is not in favor of it.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:07.379
So I would say that Biden on criminal justice,
he's just past dealing with only symptoms

00:05:07.379 --> 00:05:11.810
towards getting at some of the problems, but
it doesn't do nearly enough.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.400
Now, by the way, this is Trump's a disaster.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.450
So this is not a comparison with Trump.

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:18.080
I want to make that really clear.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.740
Next, let's look at the economy.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:20.919
Joe Biden on the economy.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:21.919
OK.

00:05:21.919 --> 00:05:24.090
What is Joe Biden's economic policy?

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.900
Joe Biden wants a $15 an hour minimum wage.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:33.699
He wants paid family and sick leave, a 1.3
trillion dollar infrastructure package.

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:38.300
Roll back the Trump tax cuts, meaning raise
the top rate from thirty seven to thirty nine

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.200
point six percent.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.259
Extend the payroll tax to $400000.

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:48.199
Currently, that caps out at about one hundred
thirty eight thousand, raise the corporate

00:05:48.199 --> 00:05:56.030
tax rate from 21 to 28 percent, tax capital
gains and dividends as ordinary income after

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:57.870
$1 million a year.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:02.599
And then put a 15 percent minimum tax on large
companies to prevent them from using loopholes

00:06:02.599 --> 00:06:05.030
and deductions to end up paying zero.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:11.379
So here Biden starts to get at some of the
actual economic problems in this country inequality,

00:06:11.379 --> 00:06:18.810
a system designed to allow you to pay less
and less as a percentage of what you earn

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.889
as you have more and more.

00:06:20.889 --> 00:06:24.030
This applies to rich individuals and corporations
as well.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.990
So Biden is getting at some of the fundamental
problems here.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:33.400
Now, what Biden doesn't deal with in terms
of problems are the absolutely sky high costs

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.879
of living in much of the country, 15 bucks
an hour.

00:06:36.879 --> 00:06:40.720
It's great, but it's not a living wage in
much of the country.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:45.889
Doesn't deal with guaranteeing a living wage,
doesn't deal with the loopholes that are disproportionately

00:06:45.889 --> 00:06:47.500
used by the super rich.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:55.270
So, for example, taking the payroll tax threshold
up to 400000 this year, it's one hundred and

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:59.659
thirty seven thousand seven hundred that hits
people earning between one hundred and thirty

00:06:59.659 --> 00:07:01.669
seven K and four hundred K.

00:07:01.669 --> 00:07:07.360
But then it goes away and we can have a debate
over what's right and what's fair and what's

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.419
economically sensible.

00:07:08.419 --> 00:07:13.419
But the point is, if you're above 400000 a
year in income, you're unaffected by that.

00:07:13.419 --> 00:07:18.500
And the ultra rich who are really benefiting
from a lot of the loopholes and mechanisms

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:22.000
that exist, they're earning way more than
$400000 a year.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.419
Another example, the top tax bracket would
go back to thirty nine point six percent under

00:07:26.419 --> 00:07:27.419
Joe Biden.

00:07:27.419 --> 00:07:29.330
That's what it was before Donald Trump.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.550
OK, great.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.789
But that doesn't go nearly high enough.

00:07:32.789 --> 00:07:35.539
And we need we need higher and more tax brackets.

00:07:35.539 --> 00:07:37.289
We probably need.

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:42.509
There's a bunch of proposals, but we probably
need like a 42 percent tax bracket at a million

00:07:42.509 --> 00:07:44.580
and then we would go to a 48 percent.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:45.580
OK.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.680
So we need more brackets and they need to
go higher.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.330
Biden does a little bit, but he's not really
dealing with it at at a more core issue, which

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:57.009
is the ultra ultra rich that as a percentage
of their total income are actually paying

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:58.509
lower rates.

00:07:58.509 --> 00:08:02.439
But there is some good stuff in there and
night and day compared to Trump.

00:08:02.439 --> 00:08:03.919
I mean, truly night and day.

00:08:03.919 --> 00:08:12.659
In short, Biden's economic policy platform
is a completely predictable, uncontroversial,

00:08:12.659 --> 00:08:15.229
moderately left proposal.

00:08:15.229 --> 00:08:16.580
It deals with symptoms.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.560
It gets some problems, but it doesn't do nearly
enough.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.330
It's way better than Trump.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.620
Let's do one more area for today, which is
health care.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.610
This is obviously huge.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.080
Biden on health care.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:35.190
He has said that he supports lowering the
Medicare age from 65 to 60, would create a

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:40.230
public option, would give free access to the
public option.

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:44.570
If you're in a state that didn't do the Medicaid
expansion that was part of Obamacare, there

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:50.030
are Republican governors who said, OK, Obamacare
includes this Medicaid expansion, but we're

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:51.030
not going to do it.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:56.210
If you are in one of those states, you would
get free access to the public option even

00:08:56.210 --> 00:09:02.820
if your state didn't do the expansion based
on income, up to 138 percent of the federal

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:03.820
poverty level.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:05.530
That's like five million people.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:12.020
And then Biden would also increase tax credits
by eliminating the 400 percent poverty level

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:18.380
cap and limiting the total out-of-pocket cost
to 8.5 percent of income.

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.620
That would be down from close to 10 percent.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:25.480
And the credits would be based on gold plans
rather than I don't remember if it's bronze

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:26.770
or silver currently.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.140
That raises the amount of the credits.

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:34.200
And then Biden would limit launch prices and
price increases on drugs as well as allow

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.020
foreign drug purchases.

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:37.090
So there's a lot there.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:39.050
It is not Medicare for all.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.050
It is not universal.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:42.030
There is no doubt about it.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:47.910
What is the numbers that that this would achieve
if you lower the Medicare age from 65 to 60?

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:50.890
I believe it adds 18 million people to Medicare.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:53.810
I don't have that number in front of me and
I had a little trouble finding it.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:57.920
But going from memory, I believe it's about
18 or 20 million more people that would get

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:59.150
Medicare by lowering.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:00.620
The age from 65 to 60.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:05.760
It's not universal, but a lot of people up
free public option in states without Medicaid

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:10.510
expansion would add again about 5 million,
4.9 million people.

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:14.770
And then there are certainly millions more
that would be able to afford health insurance.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:15.920
With this, is it a panacea?

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.280
Of course not.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.390
Of course not.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:24.460
Is it better than Trump's proposal with Republicans,
which would have seen 24 to 32 million more

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:26.170
people lose insurance?

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:27.830
Of course it's better than that.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.820
The symptoms are.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.250
Care is too expensive.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:36.700
It's sometimes low quality and it's not accessible
to everyone, in large part because of the

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.800
for profit system that we have.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:43.120
Does Biden's plan change the problem of health
care being for profit?

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.420
Of course not.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:46.440
He doesn't believe that's the problem.

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:51.490
That's a major disagreement right now, even
within the Democratic Party.

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:55.730
Biden deals substantively with symptoms.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:59.730
And the way he does it is you get care to
more people and you make it affordable for

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:00.730
more people.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.330
But not everyone.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:04.670
So let's step back a little bit.

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:10.750
To sum up, we have a system that encourages
at a fundamental level because of the frequency

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:15.550
of elections, how politics is financed, needing
to raise money, etc. and how long things take

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:16.550
to get done.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:21.090
We have a system that incentivizes appearing
to deal with symptoms.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:23.630
Sometimes you're actually dealing with a symptom.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:26.280
Sometimes you're only appearing to and optics.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:30.360
Very much are the only thing that actually
matters when Congress is up for reelection

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:31.690
every two years.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:37.300
When presidents get four year terms, we have
to understand the difficulty in a system like

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.160
that of dealing with problems.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:43.730
This doesn't excuse candidates or presidents
who don't do it, and it doesn't encourage

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:44.870
only dealing with symptoms.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.080
We just have to understand that reality.

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:53.850
Trump, by and large, has identified the wrong
symptoms and is dealing with them in a completely

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:54.850
farcical way.

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.780
That's how I would sum it up.

00:11:56.780 --> 00:12:05.560
Joe Biden would actually deal with these symptoms
in a way that would function reasonably well,

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:08.910
but would only start to get at the underlying
problems.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:13.960
That's my assessment on health care, economy
and criminal justice.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.950
We could look at environment and others and
maybe we will do so.

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:21.470
Let me know what you think about this framework
of symptoms vs. problems.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:44.850
I'm on Twitter

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:46.790
at David Pakman.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:13:22.020
We'll take

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:34.310
a quick break and so much on today's program.

